# Post-Test Cleanup — Phase B: Resolver intent (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before implementation)
# B1.1 GIVEN the same gym/company, WHEN the task-derived intent is `cancel`
#      versus `transferLocation` or `updateAddress`, THEN resolveProvider receives
#      that intent and can return distinct, intent-correct paths. The user is
#      never asked to choose resolver intent.
# B1.2 GIVEN a resolver requirement, WHEN it is returned or rendered, THEN its
#      exact HTTPS citation is included in `citations`. Any malformed or uncited
#      requirement downgrades the response to concierge and no requirement
#      renders.
# B1.3 GIVEN a cited notice-period requirement and the identity document's move
#      date, WHEN the client renders the action, THEN it shows exactly `This one
#      needs {n} days' notice — do it by {date} to be clear before your move.`
#      using moveDate minus noticeDays.
# B1.4 GIVEN two identical company + intent requests, WHEN the second request is
#      resolved, THEN it hits the company+intent cache. Different intents use
#      distinct cache documents.
# B1.5 GIVEN the current task catalog, WHEN provider resolution starts, THEN the
#      task and move context deterministically map to: financial accounts,
#      insurance, and vet/pharmacy address paths -> updateAddress; local
#      memberships -> transferLocation; long-distance memberships -> cancel;
#      vet/pharmacy current-provider paths -> transferRecords. closeAccount is
#      accepted by the resolver but currently has no catalog caller.
# B1.6 GIVEN Phase B is deployed, THEN the only deployment target is
#      `functions:resolveProvider`.
